# 006 · Docs for testers

**Status:** `DROPPED`, merged into [060](_completed/060-docs-site.goal) · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Tester basics

## What

Bring the docs up to what a first-time tester needs:

- the quick start names v0.1.0, lists every worker harness (Pi, OpenCode, Claude Code) and gives disk and memory sizes;
- a how-to for choosing a model: the free path first, then a model server on your own machine, then API keys, then subscriptions, with a warning to set a stop time or a budget before you use a paid key;
- a troubleshooting page: failed checks, port clashes, the Podman VM's disk and memory, slow builds, a full reset, and where the logs are;
- what the harness image contains, and how to extend it with `FROM`;
- how to build the images and push them to your own registry;
- a screenshot or short GIF of the dashboard in the README.

## Why

The model step and the first failure are where new testers stop.

## Done when

- [ ] Each page above exists and is linked from the docs index.
- [ ] Each page was followed once on a clean machine.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: Yes to the troubleshooting page, the own-registry how-to, the toolchain list and the screenshot.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.
